diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..891b3cf 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,28 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Delivery behavior
+
+When a subscribed event is committed, each active webhook on that board receives a background `POST` to its configured URL. Generic receivers get an `application/json` event containing `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `particulars`, `eventable`, `board`, and `creator`. Card and comment data use the corresponding API representations. Recognized Slack URLs receive a `text` message; Campfire and Basecamp chat URLs receive HTML in `content`.
+
+Requests include these headers:
+
+| Header | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `X-Webhook-Delivery` | Stable ID of the delivery, also shown in the delivery log. |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | UTC timestamp of the event. |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | Hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body, using the webhook's signing secret. |
+
+Verify the signature against the **raw request body**, before parsing or re-encoding JSON, using a constant-time comparison.
+
+Fizzy creates one delivery per webhook/event and makes a **single HTTP attempt**. Duplicate jobs cannot resend a delivery, and failures are not retried. A pending outbox entry can be recovered if enqueueing was interrupted, but an attempt that has already started is never repeated. HTTP alone cannot guarantee exactly-once processing at a receiver: a lost response or interrupted worker can leave the outcome unknown. Custom receivers should deduplicate side effects atomically using the signed event ID in the JSON body, scoped to their webhook. The delivery ID header can be used to correlate a request with its log entry, but is not covered by the body signature.
+
+Any `2xx` response counts as success. Other HTTP responses are logged as completed but failed; timeouts and network errors are logged as errored. Requests have a ten-second timeout, do not follow redirects, and can only connect to public IP addresses. Environment HTTP proxies are not used. URLs must use HTTP or HTTPS, include a host, and not contain credentials. Set `BASE_URL` to your instance's public URL so links in event payloads point back to your instance.
+
+A webhook is automatically deactivated after **at least ten consecutive failures spanning at least one hour**. A successful delivery resets both the count and the start of the failure streak. Reactivation also resets the streak. Deactivated webhooks do not receive new events, and queued deliveries that have not started are skipped, not replayed on reactivation.
+
+Delivery logs are retained for **seven days**, with expired entries removed every fifteen minutes. Failure tracking is independent of log retention.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
